  { q: 'What is the difference between gross pay and net pay?', a: 'Gross pay is what you earn before anything is withheld. Net pay, or take-home pay, is what lands in your account after deductions. The main withholdings are the 7.65% payroll tax, federal income tax, and any state income tax. Because these vary by person, a converter shows gross, which is why the Best Answer Hub Salary Converter is clear about the difference.' },
