  { q: 'What is the difference between biweekly and semi-monthly pay?', a: 'Biweekly means every two weeks, which is 26 pay periods a year. Semi-monthly means twice a month, which is 24 pay periods a year. Biweekly checks are smaller but arrive more often, and two months each year bring a third biweekly check. The Best Answer Hub Salary Converter shows both so the per-check amounts line up correctly.' },
